      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ISTHISTHEREALLIFE (3) did a good job to finish second at Kilmore two runs ago then settling back and failed to finish off well enough at her latest appearance over 2240m at Melton, beaten 10 metres into eighth. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Has the ability to take care of this field. UBETTA KNOT (1) recorded another strong performance last time when she battled on bravely to finish third over 1609m at this track. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. It doesn't get any easier but on her best form she is capable of testing her rivals. MONTANA PRIDE (4) disappointed last time when seventh over 1720m at Melton. Can turn things around. IM WESLEY (8) has been about the mark of late and must be respected, the latest offering a sound second at Shepparton over 1690m.",
